artifact.self_contained_problem:
For an integer r ≥ 6, does there exist a constant c' = c'(r) > 0 (depending only on r) such that for every positive integer m there exists a (simple, undirected) graph G with exactly m edges and girth at least r (i.e., the length of the shortest cycle in G is at least r) with the property that every bipartite subgraph of G has at most
    m/2 + c' · m^{r/(r+1)}
edges? Equivalently, the maximum cut of G satisfies mc(G) ≤ m/2 + c' · m^{r/(r+1)}.

